Package: gnome-shell-extension-clipdeck
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, gnome-shell (>= 48~), gnome-shell (<< 51~)
Description: clipboard history in the GNOME Shell top bar
 Clipdeck adds a clipboard icon to the GNOME Shell top bar. Clicking it
 shows a history of everything recently copied or cut: text, links,
 images, screenshots and files (including videos, shown with
 thumbnails).
 .
 Choosing an item puts it back on the clipboard and pastes it into the
 focused window. The history can be searched, and items can be pinned
 or removed. It is stored privately in the user's home directory, and
 items that password managers mark as secret are never recorded.
